<title>GERMANY: BASF says 1996 DVFA result at 4.40 dmk.</title>
<headline>BASF says 1996 DVFA result at 4.40 dmk.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAFEN, Germany 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group EPS (DVFA method)		  4.40    vs 3.77 dmk</p>
<p>    Group cash flow			    6,798   vs 6,368</p>
<p>    Return on assets			   11.4    vs 11.2 pct</p>
<p>    Capital expenditures		     3,639   vs 3,024</p>
<p>    Research and develpoment expenses    2,286   vs 2,088</p>
<p>    Personnel expenses			 11,025  vs 10,818</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    103,406 vs 106,565</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     4,414   vs 4,128</p>
<p>    Group sales				  48,776  vs 46,229</p>
<p>    Dividend				     1.70    vs 1.40 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German chemicals and drugs group is BASF AG. Analysts had expected a five percent rise in pre-tax profits with estimates lying between 4.30 billion and 4.369 billion marks. Sales were expected to climb about 3.5 percent to somewhere between 47.6 billion and 48.2 billion marks. The dividend was expected to rise by 20 pfennigs to 1.60 marks. BASF released several figures on March 18 after its supervisory board meeting and released some this morning ahead of a news conference.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
